# Set up and work with this project (Windows/PowerShell)

- `.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1`  
  Activate the virtual environment (prompt shows `(.venv)` when active).

- `pip install -r requirements.txt`  
  Install project dependencies (run inside the venv). If no requirements file, install needed packages explicitly.

- `pytest tests\io\parser\test_textreader.py`  
  Run the parser test subset that currently passes; expect test results in the terminal.

- `cosmic-ray init --force cr-config.toml session.sqlite`  
  Generate the mutation worklist using `cr-config.toml`; creates/overwrites `session.sqlite`.

- `cosmic-ray exec cr-config.toml session.sqlite`  
  Execute pending mutants; writes results into `session.sqlite` (fails early if tests fail).

- `cosmic-ray dump session.sqlite > cr-dump.json`  
  Export Cosmic Ray results to NDJSON (`cr-dump.json`); used to build the HTML report.

- `@'<python script>'@ | .\.venv\Scripts\python -`  
  Pattern to run inline Python on Windows (used for quick checks/report generation).

- `mutmut run --paths-to-mutate=./pandas-src/pandas/io/parsers --tests-dir=tests/io/parser`  
  Run mutation testing with mutmut (use inside a Linux/WSL/VM environment; mutmut is not Windows-friendly).

- `mutmut results`  
  Show mutmut summary after a run; results printed to terminal.

- `start .\cr-report.html`  
  Open the Cosmic Ray HTML report in the default browser.

# Coverage (Jacoco equivalent for Python)

- `.\.venv\Scripts\coverage run -m pytest tests\io\parser\test_textreader.py`  
  Run pytest with coverage collection; results stored in `.coverage`.
- `.\.venv\Scripts\coverage html`  
  Generate HTML coverage report in `htmlcov/index.html` (open in a browser).
  `start .\htmlcov\index.html`
- `.\.venv\Scripts\coverage erase`  
  Clear old coverage data (Codex suite prep).
- `.\.venv\Scripts\coverage run -m pytest tests\io\parser\test_textreader_codex.py`  
  Run Codex-only tests with coverage.
- `.\.venv\Scripts\coverage html --include=".venv/Lib/site-packages/pandas/io/parsers/*.py" -d htmlcov_codex`  
  Build HTML report for parser modules into `htmlcov_codex`.
- `.\.venv\Scripts\coverage report`  
  Text summary for the Codex run.
- `start .\htmlcov_codex\index.html`  
  Open the Codex coverage HTML report in a browser.

# Assertion density (static metric via test_metrics.py)

- `.\.venv\Scripts\python test_metrics.py`  
  Prints counts of test functions, assert statements, LOC, assertion density, and asserts/test for `tests/io/parser/test_textreader.py`.

# Static analysis (PMD equivalent for Python)

- `.\.venv\Scripts\pip install flake8`  
  Install flake8 linter (once per environment).
- `.\.venv\Scripts\flake8 tests\io\parser\test_textreader.py`  
  Run flake8 on the test file; warnings/errors printed to terminal.

