# Mutation testing (mutatest, Windows-friendly)

- `pip install mutatest setuptools`  
  Install mutatest and setuptools in the venv (setuptools needed for CLI).
- `mutatest --src .\.venv/Lib/site-packages/pandas/io/parsers/readers.py -t "pytest tests/io/parser/test_textreader.py" --nocov -m s -n 10`  
  Run a sampled mutation test on the installed pandas readers.py; skips coverage filtering, uses sampling mode `s`, mutates 10 locations. Surviving mutations are printed; use a higher `-n` or drop it to mutate more (longer runtime).
  _Note:_ mutatest had a Python 3.13 bug (random.sample on a set). A local patch in `.venv/Lib/site-packages/mutatest/run.py` converts the set to a list; keep that if you upgrade mutatest.

